This release contains two distinct license regimes:

1. CODE (everything under `code/`, plus configuration files such as
   `requirements.txt` and helper scripts at the repository root):
   MIT License (below).

2. DATA (everything under `data/`, the contents of `code/prompts/`, and the
   documentation files `README.md`, `DATASHEET.md`, `REPRODUCE.md`):
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Exception: the third-party material listed in item 3 keeps its own license.

3. THIRD-PARTY DATA from "Werewolf Among Us: Multimodal Resources for Modeling
   Persuasion Behaviors in Social Deduction Games" (Lai et al., Findings of
   ACL 2023; https://huggingface.co/datasets/bolinlai/Werewolf-Among-Us),
   redistributed under the Apache License 2.0 (full text in
   `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`):
     - `data/ego4d/splits/`             (unmodified)
     - `data/ego4d/transcripts/`        (unmodified subset)
     - `data/ego4d/metadata/game_timestamp/` (unmodified)
     - in the label CSVs: the `Timestamp`, `Speaker`, `Line` fields and the
       persuasive-strategy labels in `true_category` (labels unmodified;
       re-formatted into one comma-separated column)
     - in `vote_outcome/*.json`: `playerNames`, `startRoles`, `endRoles`,
       `votingOutcome`, `startTime`, `endTime` (modified: MIDA adds
       `nightActions` and related fields)
     - the YouTube video IDs in `data/youtube/metadata/videos_link.txt`
   Changes made by the MIDA authors are licensed under CC BY 4.0.

The underlying *raw video and audio* of the source corpora (Ego4D and YouTube)
are NOT redistributed in this release; users must obtain those materials from
the original distributors under their respective licenses (the Ego4D Terms of
Use; YouTube Terms of Service for content owned by the original uploaders).

